[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. I haven't opened the page in a browser to try it.

  - [1mMarkup:[0m a sample task, "Example task", is a [38;5;153m<label class="task">[39m holding a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m and the
    task text. Because the label wraps both, clicking the text also ticks the box.
  - [1mState:[0m the checkbox itself stores on/off. A short script adds a [38;5;153mdone[39m class to the task when it's checked and removes
    it when it's unchecked.
  - [1mStyle:[0m a done task gets strikethrough and gray text. Delete the one CSS rule if you want a plain checkbox.

  To add more tasks, copy the [38;5;153m<label class="task">…</label>[39m block. The state isn't saved, so it resets when the page
  reloads. I haven't committed the change.

